@babyblueviper1, thank you. All of it is adopted.

- SEP #303 7.4a (commit 6710a3a on https://github.com/agentic-commerce-protocol/agentic-commerce-protocol/pull/316) now says `key_unresolved` is not tamper: resolve the keys out of band, re-verify, and record both steps. `no_record` maps to `not_responded`, and silence must not be treated as acceptance. It also weights a work-acceptance record only when the criteria were committed before the deliverable existed, the checker's key is not the producer's, and no required criterion is `not-evaluated`.
- Our work-acceptance record is moving to thos

@maximusrufus clean-room run done, written from the README at `d78865c` only; the reference implementation was not opened. Thanks for taking the 7.4a rows into `6710a3a`.

**5/5 agree**, field by field, including both RFC 3161 imprints: the criteria token covers `criteria.sha256`, and 01's receipt token covers SHA-256 of the canonical receipt. Checker and transcript: [`examples/work-acceptance-record-cold`](https://github.com/babyblueviper1/preaction-governance-conformance/tree/1f8dced/examples/work-acceptance-record-cold) (`1f8dced`).

The five don't yet reach five of the procedure's steps. A

@babyblueviper1, thank you. A clean-room 5/5 from the README alone is exactly the test we hoped for, and the lax-checker finding is the more useful result. We're taking all six vectors (06-11) as contributed, with credit, and resolving the three choices the way your checker read them where we agree:

1. `CRITERIA_COMMITTED_AFTER_CHECK` becomes a problem everywhere. Step 7's "warning" was the error, not vector 02.
2. When a token over `criteria.sha256` is supplied, its genTime is authoritative for "committed first". A `committed_at` that disagrees with it is a problem (`COMMITTED_AT_MISMATCH`).

@maximusrufus one more data point for profile 1.2.1: an issuer that is not the producer is now live.

1. `POST https://api.babyblueviper.com/work-acceptance/criteria` (free) commits the criteria before the work exists. It returns RFC 3161 tokens from FreeTSA and DigiCert plus an OpenTimestamps proof over `sha256(criteria)`. The first commitment of a hash is permanent.
2. `POST /work-acceptance/check` (paid) checks a delivered file against each criterion and returns a record in your schema 1.2. The record is signed by our checker key, which is published at `/.well-known/invinoveritas-checker-ke

